        "original_id": "0081aa21-9bef-5488-bcf7-096e867a9d27",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Concepts: big cats, cat relationships, Felidae taxonomy\n- Organizations: Acinonychini\n- Systems: Puma (genus)\n- Animals: cheetahs, cougars, domestic cats, lions, leopards, jaguarundi\n- Topics: Old World fossil representatives, Pliocene Eurasia\n\nFacts:\n- In Acinonychini, cheetahs and cougars are sometimes considered big cats.\n- In Acinonychini, cheetahs and cougars are more closely related to domestic cats than to lions and leopards.\n- Puma is a genus in the family Felidae that contains the cougar, also called the puma, and the jaguarundi.\n- Puma may also include several poorly known Old World fossil representatives, including \"Puma pardoides\" or \"Owen's panther,\" a large cougar-like cat from Pliocene Eurasia.",
